	(text "Connector pinouts CONFIRMED from PiezoMotor PMD401 Technical Manual 150025-01 sec.3.4 / 3.5 (servo mode). All JST SH 1.0 mm.\nServo connector = the PMD401 6-pole sensor connector in servo mode; the LL06 encoder therefore connects to THIS board (J705).\nJ705 mirrors the PMD401 sensor-connector pinout so the kit encoder cable can plug in - VERIFY against the delivered cable.\nE-07: TVS + 100 R on every PMD401 signal line. PMD401 inputs have internal pull-ups (10k/~20k/22k) to an UNSTATED rail (IF-02).\nECO1: READY and FAULT reach the MCU through BSS138 level shifters Q701/Q702: the MCU pin never sees above 3.3 V whatever the PMD401 rail, in reset or unpowered.\nFIRMWARE: READY and FAULT both read LOW when the PMD401 is unpowered, so trust them only after FLY_PGOOD is high.\nAEN has a 22k internal pull-up (manual); it is driven open-drain by Q402 (sheet Kill path): parked unless the supervisor unparks.\nEncoder supply (OPEN item 12): JP701 default 3V3 (logic rail, survives 48 V switching); alternative PMD401 5V Out."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
